INT. FLOODED PARKING GARAGE - NIGHT

Six inches of black water cover the concrete. A broken sign sparks overhead. Pillars throw long shadows. Somewhere, a pump coughs.

LUCIANA "LUCKY" ROSSETTI (30s, wet leather jacket, nervous grin) wades toward a gray sedan, a duffel bag on her shoulder. At the car, her partner NATHANIEL "NATE" OBI (40s, calm, wire-rimmed glasses) checks the trunk.

LUCKY
Tell me it's all there.

NATE
Count it yourself.

LUCKY
I trust you.

NATE
You shouldn't.

She drops the bag in the trunk. He slams it shut. Headlights sweep across the pillars.

LUCKY
Who's that?

NATE
Nobody.

LUCKY
Nate. Who is that?

A black van rolls to a stop. The door slides open. DETECTIVE MARISOL VEGA (40s, rain slicker, badge on her belt) steps out into the water, weapon drawn.

MARISOL
Hands where I can see them! Both of you!

LUCKY
Marisol, wait, I can explain --

NATE
Don't say a word, Lucky.

MARISOL
Away from the car, Nathaniel!

NATE
It's Nate.

MARISOL
I don't care what it is!

SILAS PRINGLE (60s, garage attendant in a yellow poncho) peers around a pillar, flashlight shaking.

SILAS
Folks? We're closed. Folks?

Lucky lunges for the trunk; Nate grabs her wrist; Marisol fires a warning shot that rings off the ceiling. All three freeze, and the water ripples outward from their feet.

LUCKY
You said she wasn't coming.

NATE
I said she wasn't supposed to.

MARISOL
Last chance. Step away.

Nate lets go of Lucky. She sprints for the stairwell; Marisol swings the gun toward her, then back at Nate. He lifts his hands slowly.

NATE (CONT'D)
(quiet)
You were always better at this than me.

MARISOL
Don't flatter me. Where's she going?

NATE
Up.

Marisol lowers her gun an inch. Then raises it again. Footsteps splash away into the dark.
